Build and manage templates

Usage:
  anona-compute template [flags]
  anona-compute template [command]

Aliases:
  template, templates, tpl

Available Commands:
  build       Build a template from a Dockerfile
  delete      Delete a template (running sandboxes keep running)
  info        Show a template and its builds
  list        List your templates (--all: the built-in ones too)
  logs        Print a build's log (the newest build unless --build), following it while it runs

Flags:
  -h, --help   help for template

Global Flags:
      --api-key string             API key (env ANONA_COMPUTE_API_KEY, E2B_API_KEY)
      --api-url string             API URL (env ANONA_COMPUTE_API_URL, E2B_API_URL; default https://api.<E2B_DOMAIN>)
      --json                       JSON output on stdout (same as -o json)
  -o, --output string              output format: text or json (default "text")
      --profile string             config profile to use (env ANONA_COMPUTE_PROFILE; default "default")
      --request-timeout duration   timeout for each API request (0 = none)
  -v, --verbose                    verbose output on stderr

Use "anona-compute template [command] --help" for more information about a command.
